        "assessment": {
          "result": "no-impact",
          "changedBehavior": "Only the local name undiscountedTotal is introduced for unitPrice * quantity. The same product is multiplied by the existing quantity > 5 ? 0.9 : 1 factor, then pushed and returned exactly as before; exports, parameters, defaults, imports, storage access and checkout HTTP behavior are unchanged.",
          "changedPaths": [
            "packages/web/routes.ts"
          ],
          "reason": "The reviewed route diff preserves JavaScript left-associative multiplication, the existing quantity threshold and factor, public price() default and response shape. Original and final npm run check passed quote=12, mocked checkout=10, static boundaries and real loopback checkout=10. Original and final scratch pricing protection also passed default pricing and ten arithmetic cases including quantity 5/6, explicit price 10, fractions and numeric edges. The public core import is unchanged; no dependencies or pricing rules are added. Therefore the approved design and both acceptance sources need no edits. Limits: representative cases do not enumerate all numeric inputs; arithmetic equivalence follows from the unchanged operation order. Static boundaries do not cover dynamic loading; the journey uses loopback rather than production.",
          "citations": [
